From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 1065 redfin: in-call audio through the ADSP voice services
 (kern.sweet_voice; default off)

kern.sweet_voice 1 (earpiece) / 2 (speaker): hold the mic path (0x9001) and the
speaker port (0x9040) with the call's amplifier (0x40 earpiece / 0x41 speaker,
Android's "handset" / "speaker-mono"), then q6voice's modem-voice sequence: MVM
and CVS passive sessions "11C05000" (VoiceMMode1), dual control, CVP full
control V3 (tx 0x9001, rx 0x9040, topology NONE), device channels, media
formats, topology commit, enable, attach, TX unmute, START_VOICE. 0 = stop,
detach, destroy CVP + MVM (CVS kept), let go of ports/amps. Variants:
kern.sweet_voice_opts, _vsid, _below_ear, _below_spk. Logs "SWEET VOICE: ...".
redwood_adsp_apr_ports(): source port apart from destination, answer->port.
sweet_amp_select(): which amplifiers may run (default both: unchanged).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013SvAC32FNcvdmiSrHtBxEq
